  "note": "Razorfin Abolisher's \"target creature with a counter on it\" asks whether the candidate has a counter at all, of any kind (CR 122.1). Bob's Hill Giant carries a stun counter, deliberately not +1/+1, so a kind-specific filter admits nothing; his Goblin Piker carries none, and alice's own Abolisher is a third counterless creature. Activated naming nothing, the slot is bound unasked, which the runner allows only when it has exactly one legal answer (CR 601.2c via 602.2b): a slot admitting the Piker or the Abolisher too would raise a target prompt nothing answers and fail the run. That is the singleton the Haskell original read off the slot. The Giant goes to its owner's hand and the Piker stays.",
